# a long conflict (6th to 7th centuries)



&nbsp;

&nbsp;

the byzantines and the sasanians fought a very long war.


it lasted through the sixth and seventh centuries.


for most of this time, fighting was steady and ongoing.


there were breaks in the battles. at times, the two sides even made alliances with each other.


but for most of this period, war shaped how they related to one another.



&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

# khosrow i and the first long war



&nbsp;

&nbsp;

**khosrow i** was a strong military leader.


he stopped several attacks by nomadic peoples on the sasanian empire.


in **532**, he made a peace deal with the byzantines.


&nbsp;

that peace did not last.


while the byzantine emperor **justinian** was busy taking back italy, khosrow moved west into byzantine land.


a long war followed from **541 to 557**.


during this war, the sasanians took parts of byzantine-controlled land. these included **armenia** and **syria**.


&nbsp;

a truce was signed in **557**.


it ended in **565**, when justinian died.


fighting started again after that.



&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

