&nbsp;

&nbsp;

## germany's early successes


&nbsp;

&nbsp;

the final year of the war started well for germany.

&nbsp;

in march, german troops launched an offensive against the british. they quickly gained the advantage. poor weather and fog caused confusion on the field. the british may have retreated farther than needed.

&nbsp;

germany moved toward paris again. it resumed bombing the city. this was just like the early weeks of the war. germany also signed treaties with russia and romania. both countries left the war. they gave up land in the process.

&nbsp;

by summer 1918, germany held more land than at any point before.

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;



## the allies gain numbers


&nbsp;

&nbsp;

in that same summer, a large force of united states troops arrived. after four long years of war, france and britain welcomed the help. china and greece also joined the war. brazil entered in october 1917.

&nbsp;

other nations declared war on the central powers too. haiti, cuba, and most of central america did so between spring 1917 and summer 1918. none of these countries sent troops. none played a key role in the fighting.

&nbsp;

the central powers had done well in the first half of 1918. but now the allies had a huge number edge. their advantage was nearly three to one. the central powers could not hold out against that for long.

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;



## the meuse-argonne offensive


&nbsp;

